---
description: Aangan dropdowns use the menu pick list, not a native select
alwaysApply: true
---

# Dropdowns

Every choice list uses the menu pick. Do not add a `<select>`. The closed control matches a text field: 48px, radius 14px, paper background, saffron focus ring. The open list is cream, hover `#f6efe4`, selected row `#3d2b22` with cream text. No operating-system blue.

Styles already live in `client/src/styles.scss` (`.pick`, `.pick-btn`, `.pick-list`). Do not copy them into a component style file. A field beside Price, or any other 48px control, stays on the same row and the same height. Food type keeps the veg, non-veg, and egg dot.

```html
<span class="pick" [class.open]="openPick() === 'category'" (click)="$event.stopPropagation()">
  <button type="button" class="pick-btn" [attr.aria-expanded]="openPick() === 'category'" (click)="togglePick('category')">{{ categoryLabel() }}</button>
  @if (openPick() === 'category') {
    <ul class="pick-list">
      @for (category of categories; track category.id) {
        <li><button type="button" [class.on]="id === category.id" (click)="choose(category.id)">{{ category.name }}</button></li>
      }
    </ul>
  }
</span>
```

Stop the click on the pick so the document listener does not close it in the same turn. Close on a choice, on outside click, and on Escape. One `openPick` signal per page. The sidebar house switcher is the only dark select; leave it until that screen is edited, then use this same list.
